.\" Manpage for Simple Shell (hsh)
.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "1.0" "Simple Shell Manual Page"
.SH NAME
hsh \- Simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple UNIX command language interpreter that executes commands read from standard input or from a file. It reads user commands, parses tokenized arguments, resolves paths using the PATH variable, and executes binaries via process creation (fork/execve).

.SH INVOCATION
If invoked without arguments and standard input is attached to a terminal, 
.B hsh
displays the prompt 
.B #cisfun$ 
and waits for user input.

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell program with the status of the last executed command.
.TP
.B env
Prints all environment variables currently accessible to the process.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Upon exit, 
.B hsh
returns the status of the last command executed, or 0 if exiting cleanly via exit.

.SH ERRORS
If a command is not found, 
.B hsh
prints an error message to standard error in the following format:
.RS
\fB./hsh: line_number: command: not found\fR
.RE

